      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I can see this working really well with groups, as I'm in several groups that take group photos during events, and not everyone taking photos and printing them wants to keep them for long after the event is over.\n\nAuto deleting a specific print after leaving the instance would be nice, especially for those who really don't need to have print slots always taken up by group photos.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2026-04-17T06:40:13.699Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Prints from the VRChat camera, but they last a short amount of time. They don't take up slots in the prints gallery (limited to 64). \n\nIt could be a print that disappears from the inventory once the instance is left, but still saves to the VRChat camera folder like normal photos.\n\nOr, it could be a rotation of a small number of prints that override eachother. For example, when a new photo is taken while this mode is enabled, the oldest print is removed from access and the slots are rotated with the newest one at the beginning.\n\nThe idea is that there is always space to have a photo printed when the need strikes, but it also doesn't take up unnecessary space. For those photos that might not be taken out again, but were very neat to have in the moment.\n\nInspired by the slight frustration of having taken a really cool photo of a person/world and wanting to print to show it, but the max prints has been reached... \n\nAlso, having many world photos that are neat to show at the time, but unnecessary to \"carry\" around because they won't be shown again. \n\nI like the aesthetic and functionality of prints, such that they have a date and location stamped on them and a nice printed photo aesthetic.\n\nA possible benefit is that this could open up space in the prints inventory overall, which can reduce storage and networking overhead of having prints loaded. Of course I can't pull numbers on that, but it's a suggestion!\n\nThis is something that I've many times thought, \"I sure wish VRChat had this\", so I'm finally making a post about it!",
